            "explanation_html": "<section class=\"dtos-explanation\" aria-label=\"DTOS trade assessment\"><h3>DTOS trade assessment</h3><p class=\"tw-final-verdict\">REJECT</p><section class=\"tw-decision\" aria-label=\"Trade decision summary\"><section class=\"tw-decision-lead\" aria-label=\"Decision and next step\"><p>Why this decision: The return loses more than half the supported Market value, exceeding the existing severe-loss policy.</p><p>Next step: Do not pursue this package on the recorded evidence. Review its costs before editing.</p></section><section class=\"tw-decision-market\" aria-label=\"Current Market comparison\"><h4>Current Market</h4><div class=\"tw-market-caption\"><span>You send <b>445</b></span><span>You receive <b>20</b></span></div><div class=\"tw-market-bar\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Your counterparty receives 425 more current Market value.\"><span class=\"advantage\" style=\"flex-basis:95.699%\"></span><span class=\"disadvantage\" style=\"flex-basis:4.301%\"></span></div><p>Your counterparty receives 425 more current Market value.</p><small>Current values, not trade-date grades. Market advantage is separate from strategy and lineup impact.</small></section><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Optimal legal-lineup production falls 3.00 points per supported week; Market overpay of 425 units</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Projection evidence is Unavailable; retained numerical evidence is provisional, not freshly verified.</p><section class=\"tw-team-summary\" aria-label=\"Current projected lineup effects\"><section><h4>Your team</h4><p>Your team: Conditional Season 2026, week 2 optimal-lineup change -3.00 projected points.</p></section><section><h4>Their team</h4><p>Their team: Conditional Season 2026, week 2 optimal-lineup change +2.00 projected points.</p></section></section><p>Inspect the main drawback, edit or reevaluate this trade.</p><details class=\"tw-team-impact-details\"><summary>Both teams \u00b7 depth, costs and conditions</summary><h4>Your team</h4><p>Conditional average across supported weeks 2, 3, 4, 5: -3.00 projected points per week; not a season forecast.</p><p>Neutral Market: 445 sent / 20 received; this is value compensation, not acceptance evidence.</p><p>Projected points from eligible backups change +0.00 points per supported week.</p><p>Season 2026, week 2 reserve cover: before 7.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots); after 7.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots).</p><p>Conditional week 2 reserve-production change: +0.00 points; not an injury forecast or a second starting lineup.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Player availability is uncertain; usable replacement production is provisional.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Projection source freshness is qualified; these are conditional projections, not guaranteed production.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Original projection observations are not confirmed Fresh; replacement production remains conditional.</p><p>Other weekly reserve effects and coverage gaps are listed separately in Before and after \u00b7 both optimal lineups.</p><p>Future capital Market value: 0 sent / 20 received. Picks do not supply projected points; future outcomes are uncertain.</p><h4>Their team</h4><p>Conditional average across supported weeks 2, 3, 4, 5: +2.00 projected points per week; not a season forecast.</p><p>Neutral Market: 20 sent / 445 received; this is value compensation, not acceptance evidence.</p><p>Projected points from eligible backups change +4.00 points per supported week.</p><p>Season 2026, week 2 reserve cover: before 4.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots); after 8.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots).</p><p>Conditional week 2 reserve-production change: +4.00 points; not an injury forecast or a second starting lineup.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Player availability is uncertain; usable replacement production is provisional.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Projection source freshness is qualified; these are conditional projections, not guaranteed production.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Original projection observations are not confirmed Fresh; replacement production remains conditional.</p><p>Other weekly reserve effects and coverage gaps are listed separately in Before and after \u00b7 both optimal lineups.</p><p>Future capital Market value: 20 sent / 0 received. Picks do not supply projected points; future outcomes are uncertain.</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Their recorded direction is WIN NOW; it does not prove willingness to accept this offer.</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Market fairness and receiving a pick do not establish rebuilding intent or predict acceptance.</p><p>This package is rejected under the recorded assessment: User-side conclusion from separate Market, optimal-lineup, package, capital and strategy evidence; counterparty plausibility is separate. Evidence gaps do not remove that objection.</p><p>This is not a qualified recommendation. Inspect the stated Market, roster and counterparty blockers before considering a package change.</p><p>Their principal cost: Spends 20 Market units of future capital</p></details><details class=\"tw-player-facts\"><summary>Player production, projections and rank definitions</summary><section><h4>Veteran producer</h4><p>QB \u00b7 NFL team unavailable \u00b7 Age 32.0 \u00b7 Unknown</p><p>Listed position eligibility: QB. Availability and roster rules are assessed separately in the legal lineup.</p><p>Market positional rank: QB1 \u00b7 Priced rostered players in the selected league.</p><p>Current Market: 445.</p><p>Sleeper projection: 10.00 \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Week 2 \u00b7 Unavailable.</p><p>Sleeper actual production: Unavailable points per completed-week score observation \u00b7 Unknown observations \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Selected league. This is not a games-played average.</p><p>Season fantasy-points rank / points-per-game rank: unavailable; no complete compatible cohort is prepa